.TH CDED 1
.SH NAME
cded \\- detect and optionally drain sensitive clipboard content
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cded
cded [--input FILE] [--allow-process NAME] [--drain]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Detects sensitive clipboard patterns. Clearing clipboard content is selected explicitly with --drain.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBcded --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
